{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= (shape(x) = shape(y)) ∨ (ndim(x) = 0) ∨ (ndim(y) = 0)
>>
Rule 9 (Ensure x's dtype is not bool.)
{x : tensor} |= dtype_(x) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 10 (x and y must have compatible shapes when both are tensors.)
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= if ndim(x) > 0 ∧ ndim(y) > 0 then shape(x) = shape(y)
>>
Rule 13 (If x or y is scalar, shape check can be skipped)
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= if ndim(x) = 0 ∨ ndim(y) = 0 then true else shape(x) = shape(y)
>>
Rule 14 (Shapes must be equal unless one is a scalar)
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= (ndim(x) = 0) ∨ (ndim(y) = 0) ∨ (shape(x) = shape(y))
>>
Rule 18 (Valid dtypes for x and y)
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= (dtype_(x) = 7 ∨ dtype_(x) = 8 ∨ dtype_(x) = 9 ∨ dtype_(x) = 4 ∨ dtype_(x) = 5 ∨ dtype_(x) = 10 ∨ dtype_(x) = 11) ∧ (dtype_(y) = 7 ∨ dtype_(y) = 8 ∨ dtype_(y) = 9 ∨ dtype_(y) = 4 ∨ dtype_(y) = 5 ∨ dtype_(y) = 10 ∨ dtype_(y) = 11)
>>
Rule 21 (x and y must have compatible dtypes and not be bool)
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= (dtype_(x) = 7 ∨ dtype_(x) = 8 ∨ dtype_(x) = 9 ∨ dtype_(x) = 4 ∨ dtype_(x) = 5 ∨ dtype_(x) = 10 ∨ dtype_(x) = 11) ∧ (dtype_(y) = 7 ∨ dtype_(y) = 8 ∨ dtype_(y) = 9 ∨ dtype_(y) = 4 ∨ dtype_(y) = 5 ∨ dtype_(y) = 10 ∨ dtype_(y) = 11) ∧ (dtype_(x) ≠ 0)
>>
Rule 27 (If x and y are tensors of same rank, then their shapes have to match.)
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= if ndim(x) > 0 ∧ ndim(y) > 0 then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(x) - 1] : shape(x, i) = shape(y, i))
>>
Rule 32 (Allowed dtypes for x and y, and x cannot be bool)
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= (dtype_(x) = 7 ∨ dtype_(x) = 8 ∨ dtype_(x) = 9 ∨ dtype_(x) = 4 ∨ dtype_(x) = 5 ∨ dtype_(x) = 10 ∨ dtype_(x) = 11) ∧ (dtype_(y) = 7 ∨ dtype_(y) = 8 ∨ dtype_(y) = 9 ∨ dtype_(y) = 4 ∨ dtype_(y) = 5 ∨ dtype_(y) = 10 ∨ dtype_(y) = 11) ∧ dtype_(x) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 40 (If both are tensors and shapes aren't equal, at least one must have dimension size 1)
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= if (ndim(x) > 0) ∧ (ndim(y) > 0) ∧ (shape(x) ≠ shape(y)) then ((∃i ∈ [0, ndim(x) - 1] : shape(x, i) = 1) ∨ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(y) - 1] : shape(y, i) = 1))
>>
Rule 43 (If both inputs are tensors and shapes aren't equal, at least one must have all dimension sizes as 1)
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= if (ndim(x) > 0) ∧ (ndim(y) > 0) ∧ (shape(x) ≠ shape(y)) then ((∀i ∈ [0, ndim(x) - 1] : shape(x, i) = 1) ∨ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(y) - 1] : shape(y, i) = 1))
>>
Rule 47 (If one is a scalar, then other shape should be a valid shape (positive dimension sizes))
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= if ndim(x) = 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(y)-1] : shape(y,i) > 0 else if ndim(y) = 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(x)-1] : shape(x,i) > 0
>>
Rule 50 (If both are tensors and shapes are not equal, either both should be of same rank or dimension sizes must be 1 for broadcasting support)
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= if (ndim(x) > 0) ∧ (ndim(y) > 0) ∧ (shape(x) ≠ shape(y)) then ((ndim(x) = ndim(y)) ∨ ((∀i ∈ [0, ndim(x) - 1] : shape(x, i) = 1) ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(y) - 1] : shape(y, i) = 1)))
>>
Rule 53 (if ndim is not 0 and dimension sizes are not equal then they should be of same rank)
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= if (ndim(x) > 0) ∧ (ndim(y) > 0) ∧ (shape(x) ≠ shape(y)) then (ndim(x) = ndim(y))
>>
Rule 54 (If either one has ndim=0, the rest should comply with valid dimension size)
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= if ndim(x) = 0 then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(y) - 1] : shape(y, i) > 0) else if ndim(y) = 0 then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(x) - 1] : shape(x, i) > 0)
>>
Rule 60 (if either of the tensor has more dimension, the other should have atleast one shape dimension 1 to allow broadcasting )
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= if (ndim(x) > 0) ∧ (ndim(y) > 0) ∧ (ndim(x) ≠ ndim(y)) then ((ndim(x) > ndim(y) ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(y)-1] : shape(y,i) = 1)) ∨ (ndim(y) > ndim(x) ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(x)-1] : shape(x,i) = 1)))
>>
Rule 63 (Check for broadcasting support.If rank are different then atleaset one of the shape at some dimension has to be 1.)
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= if (ndim(x) > 0) ∧ (ndim(y) > 0) ∧ (shape(x) ≠ shape(y)) then ((ndim(x) = ndim(y)) ∨ ((ndim(x) > ndim(y) ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(y)-1] : shape(y,i) = 1)) ∨ (ndim(y) > ndim(x) ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(x)-1] : shape(x,i) = 1))))
>>
Rule 66 (If one of the shapes has dimension > 0 but has shape length other than 1.)
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= if (ndim(x) > 0) ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(x)-1] : shape(x,i) ≠ 1) then ∀j ∈ [0, ndim(x)-1] : shape(x,j) > 0 else if (ndim(y) > 0) ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(y)-1] : shape(y,i) ≠ 1) then ∀j ∈ [0, ndim(y)-1] : shape(y,j) > 0
